%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: banneredmaregangsallhere 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559232
    - rid: 9079474820206559233
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: What to do first...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559299
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, let's start with the "how we got here part."
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, going in a circle, I want everyone to talk about what they were
      last doing before ending up here.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559285
    - rid: 9079474820206559286
    - rid: 9079474820206559287
    - rid: 9079474820206559288
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'I''ll start:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: If I remember right, I had a completely ordinary go-to-bed routine, fell
      asleep, and then -next thing I knew- I was in the cart from the opening of
      the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Um, I wasn't doing anything strange either, I just got ready for bed,
      went to sleep, and woke up in Farengar's room.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sayori?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh... I don't <i>think</i> I did anything weird either, I just woke up
      in the Temple of Kenny.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559289
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You mean the Temple of Kynareth?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, that one!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559290
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Monika?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559291
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... I was trying to find a way to get to <b>you</b> without that thing
      noticing...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559292
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (But, I have a few reasons to assume that this isn't my fault.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559293
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (First of all, I didn't make any changes to anything yesterday, I was
      just looking through the files.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Second, I don't have any of my powers here, which would be strange if
      I had the power to hop to a different dimension.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Third, that entity seems to have more power than me, so if it's anyone's
      fault, it should be them.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559294
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... you mean for this?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (If its motivation really is <i>just</i> to tell a story, then I guess
      it warped us here for that purpose?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Monika hasn't said anything for about a minute now...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, Monika? You're spacing out...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Huh? Oh, yeah.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559295
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry. The only thing of note that I remember was just being at home,
      getting some final prep work for the festival before heading to bed.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hmm. Natsuki?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559296
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559297
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Come on, Natsuki, this is to try and figure out how we got here, we need
      all the information we can get.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I don't want to talk about it.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559300
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... is her home life seriously that bad?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Fine, but do you remember anything... mystical, I guess? Unusual in the
      supernatural sense.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: No.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... alright.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So major take away: this makes no sense.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's talk about what first happened when we woke up.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Like I previously mentioned, I woke up in the cart where the player character
      wakes up in the start of the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Teehee~!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559301
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: What's so funny, Monika?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, don't worry about it. I just remembered something funny.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559302
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Wait, game? What do you mean?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559303
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, right, I should probably explain that.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Well, the world we''ve found ourselves in is pretty much exactly like
      a game I''ve played called: Skyrim.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: The game is named after the province it takes place in?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, yes, it's part of a larger series; the fifth entry to be specific.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, the major story events are playing out like how they do in-game,
      so it's safe to operate under the assumption that we're in the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Or something like that.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: So we've been isekai'd into the world of Skyrim?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: That's...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess so?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: You know, I've always thought about what I'd do if I was in an isekai...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559304
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But now that it's happened to you, you don't know what to do?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Haha... yeah...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, back on topic, Yuri?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559307
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Like I said, I woke up in Farengar's room, who is the court wizard for
      the Jarl here in Whiterun. He called me his apprentice.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sayori?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: I woke up in the Temple of Kinnyreth-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Kynareth.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559305
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, I was woken up by an older woman, who called me apprentice too,
      telling me to heal people.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559306
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... huh! Monika?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I woke up in the palace up on that hill-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You mean Dragonsreach? Where the Jarl is?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: If that's what it's called, then yes.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, I was wearing this uniform, and a guard came up to me calling
      me captain.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Interesting! Natsuki?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: I woke up in a stinky cave with some ugly-looking punks, they kept calling
      me boss even though I had no idea who any of them were.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559308
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Were they bandits?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That's what the guards called them, so yes.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ...!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, I think I see the pattern here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So, to summarize:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I woke up where the main character should be.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri and Sayori woke up near a plot-relevant character here in Whiterun.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Monika woke up replacing a pre-existing character who isn't <i>that</i>
      plot relevant.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And Natsuki woke up replacing a generic enemy character.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Based on this, it seems that we weren't just dragged here from our world.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: No, we've been integrated into this world, with backstories being given
      to us.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Whether that means mantling a pre-existing character, or being directly
      connected to one.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, {mc}, what does that mean?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559309
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... crap, I didn't think that far ahead...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess that whatever happened to us was deliberate, then?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Because if it was just some freak coincidence, we would still be in our
      pajamas, and no one would recognize us, right?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Huh! {mc}'s actually a pretty clever cookie.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559310
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Should I tell him the truth, then?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559311
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559312
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559315
    - rid: 9079474820206559313
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That's an interesting point, {mc}. Although we still don't have enough
      information to know if that's true or not.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559314
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah... you're right.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, next order of business-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559316
    - rid: 9079474820206559317
    - rid: 9079474820206559318
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Hey, who made you leader, anyway?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559319
    - rid: 9079474820206559320
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, what-?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: You're running this show like a meeting! Why are you bossing us around!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559321
    - rid: 9079474820206559323
    - rid: 9079474820206559324
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, Natsuki-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559322
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: We're in a dangerous place far from home, and you think that you should
      just take charge?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: What, just because we're a bunch of girls?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: To be fair, I thought I was the only one who's played Skyrim before-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: We never voted on that! We never agreed to that!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559325
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I was just trying to make sure everyone's on the same page-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: You didn't ask! You just said we were going here!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Monika said she was hungry, and no else said anything, so-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Probably because, oh I don't know, we don't know what's happening and
      we're scared!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm just trying to help-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, well, you should've-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: SHUT <NoiseText=3,1>UP</NoiseText>, NATSUKI!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559327
    - rid: 9079474820206559328
    - rid: 9079474820206559329
    - rid: 9079474820206559330
    - rid: 9079474820206559331
    - rid: 9079474820206559333
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: '!!!'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I've never heard Sayori scream like that... I-I-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I think I'm scared...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: '{mc} was just helping us, he w-was trying to learn about what happened
      to us...'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559334
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: He was d-doing a good thing... a-and... a-and...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Sayori's burst of rage has seemed to peter out a bit, leaving only sadness
      in its wake.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559332
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... no one wants to break the silence that followed.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Monika does her best to try and calm Sayori down.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559335
    - rid: 9079474820206559338
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Thanks Monika, very cool.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... okay, so what happened? What's her problem?!?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah, right. She did let it slip during her rant that she was scared.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: And if my experience with her at the club is anything to go by, Natsuki
      lashes out when she's scared.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: God, what a hassle-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Oh wow, maybe she has a point about me just making myself leader without
      asking...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I just thought about trying to <i>deal with her</i>, as if that's my
      responsibility.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... alright, I think I know where to go from here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Look, I wasn't trying to be some sort of brave hero or anything...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I was just trying to make the most sense out of our current situation.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Because you're right about this being scary.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Honestly, I'm scared too, and I know a lot more about this game than
      you guys do.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, I can't say that I fully understand how you're feeling, but-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But I'm sorry I didn't help you in the way that you wanted or needed.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559336
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I-I'm horrible...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559337
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: H-hey... no one said that, no one thinks that...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: B-but... you didn't deserve that at all... S-Sayori's right...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki, as annoying as it is to be on the receiving end of something
      like that, I...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't blame you for it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: W-why wouldn't y-you...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Because, Natsuki: we''re all scared.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't have the right to judge you good or bad, we're all in this together.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hey, you wanna read some-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, right. No manga in Skyrim.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Heh, you dummy...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559339
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I wasn't trying to be funny, but that seemed to help her a little.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, while I would like to get back on track, in the spirit of equality,
      does anyone else have a suggestion?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559340
    - rid: 9079474820206559341
    - rid: 9079474820206559342
    - rid: 9079474820206559343
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'll take the silence as a no, if that's alright with everybody.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, the next thing I think we should do is take stock of our resources.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Obviously, I can see that we all have at least one set of clothing, with
      three of us having armor, and the other two having robes.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri and I have around 200 septims combined, which are gold coins that
      are the currency here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: What about the rest of you?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559397
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The other three girls count their coin, which results in us having around
      [Gold] septims total.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559344
    - rid: 9079474820206559345
    - rid: 9079474820206559346
    - rid: 9079474820206559347
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Natsuki had the most, which I suppose is due to the occupation she found
      herself with.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559348
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, does everyone have a weapon?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I've got a bow, some arrows, and this sword.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559349
    - rid: 9079474820206559350
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: I've got this big, dumb hammer.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: How did I not notice her hammer? It's taller than her!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Um, I don't think I have one... but I can conjure a dagger...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559351
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: What kind of thing is this, {mc}?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559352
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Sayori pulls out what appears to be an iron mace.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, that'd be a mace. Which counts.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: So, do I just hit people with it?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Pretty much, yeah.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Hmm.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559353
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Sayori doesn't seem too thrilled by that.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: She never liked hurting people; even when she accidentally hurt someone
      she used to go into hysteria.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Look, I''m just gonna come clean:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I've personally killed at least two people already-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: In self-defense, of course!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Fighting is how most people resolve their conflict in these lands, so
      even if it's hard, it's better to be good at it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, equipment sorted, I know Yuri can do magic, but can anyone else?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: How would we know if we could?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559354
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, Yuri, how does it feel to use magic?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Like the very essence of aetherius is coursing through me...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559355
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... yeah...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Look, just try to shoot some fire out of your hands, or something.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The other three girls each try to do something...?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559356
    - rid: 9079474820206559357
    - rid: 9079474820206559358
    - rid: 9079474820206559359
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The only one who seems to have some sort of success is Sayori, whose
      hands start glowing yellow.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559360
    - rid: 9079474820206559361
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Ehehe~! That tickles!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559362
    - rid: 9079474820206559363
    - rid: 9079474820206559364
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess we found our white mage...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: So, how does magic work, anyway?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559365
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... that's a loaded question.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you want the short answer, or the Yuri answer?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri answer-? What?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559366
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: This place has a lot of lore, most of which only Yuri would probably
      care about.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: The short answer then, I guess...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, in the game you use mana points to cast spells.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559367
    - rid: 9079474820206559368
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Stronger spells cost more mana, which will usually require either leveling
      your mana stat, or increasing your skill with that type of magic.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Spells are categorized into a few different types: Destruction, Restoration,
      Alteration, Illusion, and Conjuration.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Destruction hurts people, usually with fire, frost, or lightning.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Restoration heals people, which is probably what Sayori can do.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alteration changes the physical properties of something, like making
      your skin more resistant to damage.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Illusion changes the perception of a person, so basically you can alter
      their mental state.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And Conjuration summons things from Oblivion, which is a whole other
      can of worms. Yuri uses this kind of magic to get her dagger.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: So, why can only Sayori and Yuri use magic?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Everyone has a different aptitude for certain schools of magic, and also
      separate baselines for their magicka reserve.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: It's probable that the rest of us just have a small magicka pool to draw
      from, so not enough to cast even the simplest of spells.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: This friggin' sucks, magic exists but I can't even use it...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559369
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean we can technically use it, just not to any meaningful effect.
      For now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: In the game, getting better with skills lets you increase your stats,
      including mana, so maybe we'll be able to use magic later.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, {mc}?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559370
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, Sayori?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm really hungry, can we eat now?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sure, why not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Yaay~!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559371
    - rid: 9079474820206559372
    - rid: 9079474820206559373
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I flag down Saadia to take our order.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559374
    - rid: 9079474820206559375
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: She asks what we'd like to drink, to which of course the girls have no
      idea what's available.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559376
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I ask her about the selection of drinks available for today.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ale, Alto Wine, Black-Briar Mead, Honningbrew Mead, Nord Mead, and Wine.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559377
    - rid: 9079474820206559378
    - rid: 9079474820206559379
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Not a single soft-drink! ... I could've sworn milk was an option...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Yuri asks more about the two wines.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Turns out, the Alto Wine is supposed to be sweeter. Go figure!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Yuri orders the Alto Wine.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559410
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The other three seem a bit uncomfortable with ordering booze.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: As a solution, I ask Saadia to bring all of us our own mugs, and order
      an ale, Honningbrew Mead, and a normal wine.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559411
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: That way, we can each try a little bit to see which is the most appetizing.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559380
    - rid: 9079474820206559381
    - rid: 9079474820206559382
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: This seems to satisfy everyone.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Turns out, the Honningbrew Mead is the most popular item among the girls
      by far.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559383
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The sweetness really does help balance out the taste of booze.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Saadia comes back, asking what we want to eat.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: There's a lot more options when it comes to food, but she gives us some
      recommendations.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Monika orders a salmon stew, Natsuki orders grilled chicken breast and
      a baked potato, and Yuri orders a beef stew.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559412
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Sayori, ever the munchkin, orders a baked potato, some cooked venison,
      buttered bread, and a boiled-creme tart.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559413
    - rid: 9079474820206559415
    - rid: 9079474820206559416
    - rid: 9079474820206559417
    - rid: 9079474820206559418
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Punk.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I just go for some tomato soup, since I already had a carrot.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559409
    - rid: 9079474820206559419
    - rid: 9079474820206559420
    - rid: 9079474820206559421
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: We manage to have a lovely lunch without incident, even if we now only
      have [Gold] septims.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559414
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: That was good!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm honestly surprised, considering this place doesn't have a modern
      kitchen.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559422
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Now now, Natsuki, you know you don't need a good kitchen to make good
      food, right?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559423
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh... I wonder what sort of exotic and wonderful spices they must have
      used...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559424
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Uhh... I think Yuri's a little <i>too</i> excited over something like
      spices...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: What is she, the Netherlands?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm happy we all could enjoy lunch, but uh...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559425
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's still a few things we should go over.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559426
    - rid: 9079474820206559427
    - rid: 9079474820206559428
    - rid: 9079474820206559429
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: We just spent, like, 70 septims on just lunch.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So either we need to figure out an income, or get a farm or something.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: What kind of jobs are even out here?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559430
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Few that are salaried...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's military, or we could pick up a trade.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: A trade?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559431
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well yeah, weapons and armor are pretty much always a hot commodity,
      so smithing and mining are valuable occupations.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You can't go wrong with enchanting or alchemy, either.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Eh?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alchemy is making potions or poisons, while enchanting is imbuing something
      (usually armor, clothes, or weapons) with magically properties.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: ... that sounds hard...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559432
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, maybe?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: In the game, those two are abstracted away as menu prompts.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, money's one of our problems.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The more things change, the more they stay the same...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, yeah, also dragons.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559433
    - rid: 9079474820206559434
    - rid: 9079474820206559436
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... what?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah. Dragons.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559437
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The main quest of the game revolves around the dragons coming back, terrorizing
      Skyrim...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And the biggest, baddest dragon of all, Alduin, is trying to destroy
      the world.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ... why didn't you mention that earlier?!?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559435
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki, in my defense, there's a lot to unpack about our situation right
      now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, Alduin does get defeated by the end of the story, but he's slain
      by the Last Dragonborn.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: The Last Dragonborn?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The player character in the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I told you guys that I took his place when I woke up, so either I'm him,
      or the world is doomed.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... uh, how do we know if you're the Last Dragonborn, {mc}?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, it happens fairly early in the story of the game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Basically, after the player gets the Dragonstone, a dragon attacks a
      tower in Whiterun hold.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The player and a bunch of guards kill it, and afterwards the player absorbs
      its soul.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is how the player discovers they're Dragonborn; only Dragonborns
      can eat dragon souls.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, we were going to get the Dragonstone before we ran into everyone
      else, weren't we?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That's true.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So, the basic run-down on that:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's a Nordic tomb up on a mountain south of here that has a special
      rock in it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That special rock is part of the main quest, but we'll have to go through
      some serious opposition to get to it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Why the hell would we put ourselves in danger?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, ignoring the potential end of the world happening while we're here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's technically gold to be had...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: We can loot the bandits and the gold left behind by the Nordic ancestors.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Also, there's a clean 100 or so septims involved with returning an item
      to a merchant that we can find in there.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri and I were already planning on going there, but with all five of
      us, we should have even better odds.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: '{mc}, I don''t know if that''s a good idea... we could really get hurt...'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559438
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: You have to be crazy if you think I'm going to go die in some scary tomb
      just because-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559439
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, {mc}. Let's go.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559440
    - rid: 9079474820206559441
    - rid: 9079474820206559442
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: M-Monika...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: What the hell, Monika? You can't be serious!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I'd rather go down swinging than the literal end of the world, thank
      you very much.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Besides, {mc} knows the most about this place. I don't hear any better
      ideas coming from you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm pretty familiar with the Barrow from the game, so I should probably
      be able to point out any traps.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Not that they're that well hidden, anyway.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I make no promises about the draugr, though...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But, hey! We've got five of us, and a resident healer!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That's way more than the player character gets by this point of the game!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Huh?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The healer's you, Sayori.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, okay!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559443
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: You all suck.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559444
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, if you just want to hang around here, I don't think anyone's
      going to stop you...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But it would definitely be better to stay as a group for now, and especially
      <i>not</i> go alone.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ... whatever.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474820206559445
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: That's probably about as good as we're getting from her...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Alright. Next destination: Bleak Falls Barrow.'
    ScreenActions: []
